# CASCADE local Switch configuration example — NO REAL TOKENS IN GIT.
# The offline engine (npm run demo / npm test) does not need any of these.
# The Node recovery CLI reads process environment variables; it does NOT
# automatically source this file. Export the values in your shell or inject
# them through your local Switch operations runtime.
#
# Example PowerShell:
#   $env:CASCADE_SWITCH_URL="http://localhost:59113"
#   $env:CASCADE_SWITCH_TOKEN="<YOUR_LOCAL_BOT_SERVICE_TOKEN>"
#   $env:CASCADE_SWITCH_CHANNEL_ID="<YOUR_MATTERMOST_CHANNEL_ID>"
#
# CASCADE_SWITCH_URL=http://localhost:59113
# CASCADE_SWITCH_TOKEN=
# CASCADE_SWITCH_CHANNEL_ID=
#
# The Switch Python operation can alternatively load a private environment
# file from CASCADE_BOT_ENV; keep that file OUTSIDE the tracked repo.
# CASCADE_BOT_ENV=
#
# The Switch operations registration may require the local clone location.
# CASCADE_REPO_DIR=
#
# Never put your Google OAuth token, human-account PAT, or real bot key here.
